title: WaterTemple.Entrance
---
Molly: So this looks like a door, but there's no keyhole or buttons or levers or anything.
Molly: Any idea how we open this thing?
King's Ghost: Unfortunately, I have no idea. It has never been closed off before!
MollY: Hmmm...
===
title: WaterTemple.Start
---
Molly: Well this may be the least scary place I've seen so far!
Molly: Look at all of those cool waterfalls and stuff!
Molly: Whoever built this place had some art skills.
King's Ghost: Well I am glad to see you can appreciate our Athelgardian architecture.
KIng's Ghost: My great, great grandfather commissioned this temple over two centuries ago.
King's Ghost: Only the finest artisans were summoned for its construction.
King's Guard: Only the best would be suitable to pay tribute to Ah'Qwameni.
Molly: Aqua-whoosa-watsit?
King's Guard: Ah'Qwameni, the familiar of water.
King's Ghost: Sadly, given what we've seen in our prior encounters, the rest of our visit here will less than pleasant.
Molly: Bummer.
King's Ghost: ?
===
title: WaterTemple.Questions
---
Molly: So what am I looking for here, exactly?
Molly: What does this Aqua...
Molly: Aqua...
King's Ghost: Ah'Qwameni...
Molly: Yeah, that. What does Aqua-whatever look like?
King's Ghost: It takes the form of a majestic sea-snake (maybe).
King's Ghost: But who knows what twisted form has been cast upon it now?
Molly: Well I'm sure we will know it when we see it.
Molly: Just look for the gross mash-up of two animals that have no right to be sharing a body.
King's Ghost: Indeed.
===